WEBVTT

00:03.600 --> 00:05.837
Catch code problems before they ship.

00:05.887 --> 00:08.540
This is ESLint in WaveMaker Studio.

00:09.290 --> 00:12.735
Switch ESLint on under Build Preferences.

00:12.785 --> 00:15.171
Each rule has a severity:

00:15.221 --> 00:17.050
off, warn, or error.

00:17.800 --> 00:19.934
To add a rule, choose it,

00:19.984 --> 00:23.430
set its severity, and Studio
fills in the description.

00:24.180 --> 00:26.598
Need a rule from an ESLint plugin?

00:26.648 --> 00:29.576
Add the plugin from npm under Plugins.

00:29.626 --> 00:32.210
Studio warns you if one is missing.

00:32.960 --> 00:37.035
For everything else, Advanced
Configuration opens the full config file,

00:37.085 --> 00:39.060
shared by all profiles.

00:39.810 --> 00:43.166
The Issues tab lists every problem
by file,

00:43.216 --> 00:45.450
and takes you to the exact line.

00:46.200 --> 00:48.055
Errors don't get past you.

00:48.105 --> 00:50.263
A push stops right in Studio,

00:50.313 --> 00:54.560
and builds, exports and deployments
fail until they're fixed.

00:55.310 --> 00:57.341
Because the rules live in your project,

00:57.391 --> 01:00.695
your CI/CD pipeline runs the same check,

01:00.745 --> 01:02.950
and fails the build on errors.

01:03.700 --> 01:06.659
Warnings never block,
so start with warnings

01:06.709 --> 01:10.010
and raise rules to error
as your code gets clean.

01:10.760 --> 01:13.025
ESLint in WaveMaker Studio.

01:13.075 --> 01:14.490
Ship with confidence.
